# Careers@GFTV, documentation site.
#
# Copy this file to .env.local for local development, and set the same
# variables in the Vercel project settings for preview and production.
# .env.local is gitignored. This file is committed and must never hold a real
# value.
#
# **This is a second Vercel project on the same repository**, with its root
# directory set to docs-site. Vercel builds each project from its own root and
# reads only the variables set on that project, so nothing here is inherited
# from the portal's project even though both live in one repository and read one
# Supabase project. Setting a value on one of them sets it on one of them.
#
# Every variable below is required. If one is missing the functions fail at
# import time with a message naming it, instead of throwing an undefined key
# error deep inside a request.
#
# The portal's FORM_WEBHOOK_SECRET, CRON_SECRET and TELEGRAM_BOT_USERNAME are
# deliberately not here. Nothing on this site answers a Google Apps Script, runs
# a cron, or talks to Telegram.

# Supabase project URL.
# Supabase dashboard, Project Settings, Data API, Project URL.
# The same project as the portal, not a new one: the accounts this site signs
# in are the gftvhello_users rows the portal reads.
SUPABASE_URL=https://xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx.supabase.co

# Supabase service role key. Server side only, never sent to the browser.
# Supabase dashboard, Project Settings, API Keys, service_role.
# Bypasses row level security, so treat it like a database password.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_KEY=eyJhbGciOi...

# Public base URL of this site, no trailing slash.
# Used for the cookies, and as the expected origin when a passkey response is
# verified, per 5e.
# Locally this is http://localhost:3001, so the two sites can run side by side.
DOCS_URL=https://docs.careers.globalfurry.tv

# The portal, no trailing slash. **Not this site.**
# Used for the cross links in section 16, the sign in redirects, and as the
# WebAuthn relying party id, per 5e. A passkey registered on the portal works
# here because both sites claim the portal's host as the relying party id, and
# pointing this at the docs site breaks every one of them.
# Locally this is http://localhost:3000, which makes the relying party id
# "localhost" on both sites, which is what lets a local passkey work on both.
SITE_URL=https://careers.globalfurry.tv
